{"key":"e61e2396942bc50f","source_file":"Potts Sh - So.json","source_id":25912,"source_url":"concordance-singly-ppl-singillatim","term":"Singly","headwords":["Singly"],"latin":["Singillatim","Singulatim"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Singly"],"latin":["Singillatim","Singulatim"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","CanonsNC","DLW","DP"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1662","subsection":"end"},"text":"Occurs.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLW","section":"174","subsection":null},"text":"The atmospheres are... least forms (which) receive the Sun singly. DLW 174:end.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLW","section":"279","subsection":null},"text":"The Angels perceive singly the things from the man's mind in an act.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLW","section":"378","subsection":null},"text":"This (proposition) is not so evident singly.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"124","subsection":null},"text":"The Lord never acts into any particular with man singly. Explained. DP 125.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"124","subsection":"3"},"text":"The Lord also acts into every particular of man singly; nay, most singularly; but at the same time through all things of his form...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"219","subsection":null},"text":"These points must be illustrated singly. TCR 758.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"726","subsection":"3"},"text":"Modified singly, they give light.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"CanonsNC","section":"33","subsection":null},"text":"Holy Spirit. 1. 7. Subsist not singly, but conjointly.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"singly","url":"/meta/potts/singly/"}